75","475","477","477","479","479","481","481","483","483","485","485","487","487","489","489","491","491","493","493","495","495","497","497","499","499","501","501","503","503","505","505","507","507","509","509","511","511","513","513","515","515","517","517","519","519","521","521","523","523","525","525","527","527","529","529","531","531","533","533","535","535","537","537","539","539","541","541","543","543","545","545","547","547","549","549","551","551","553","553","555","555","557","557","559","559","561","561","563","563","565","565","567","567","569","569","571","571","573","573","575","575","577","577","579","579","581","581","583","583","585","585","587","587","589","589","591","591","593","593","595","595","597","597","599","599","601","601","603","603","605","605","607","607","609","609","611","611","613","613","615","615","617","617","619","619","621","621","623","623","625","625","627","627","629","629","631","631","633","633","635","635","637","637","639","639","641","641","643","643","645","645","647","647","649","649","651","651","653","653","655","655","657","657","659","659","661","661","663","663","665","665","667","667","669","669","671","671","673","673","675","675","677","677","679","679","681","681","683","683","685","685","687","687","689","689","691","691","693","693","695","695","697","697","699","699","701","701","703","703","705","705","707","707","709","709","711","711","713","713","715","715","717","717","719","719","721","721","723","723","725","725","727","727","729","729","731","731","733","733","735","735","737","737","739","739","741","741","743","743","745","745","747","747","749","749","751","751","753","753","755","755","757","757","759","759","761","761","763","763","765","765","767","767","769","769","771","771","773","773","775","775","777","777","779","779","781","781","783","783","785","785","787","787","789","789","791","791","793","793","795","795","797","797","799","799","801","801","803","803","805","805","807","807","809","809","811","811","813","813","815","815","817","817","819","819","821","821","823","823","825","825","827","827","829","829","831","831","833","833","835","835","837","837","839","839","841","841","843","843","845","845","847","847","849","849","851","851","853","853","855","855","857","857","859","859","861","861","863","863","865","865","867","867","869","869","871","871","873","873","875","875","877","877","879","879","881","881","883","883","885","885","887","887","889","889","891","891","893","893","895","895","897","897","899","899","901","901","903","903","905","905","907","907","909","909","911","911","913","913","915","915","917","917","919","919","921","921","923","923","925","925","927","927","929","929","931","931","933","933","935","935","937","937","939","939","941","941","943","943","945","945","947","947","949","949","951","951","953","953","955","955","957","957","959","959","961","961","963","963","965","965","967","967","969","969","971","971","973","973","975","975","977","977","979","979","981","981","983","983","985","985","987","987","989","989","991","991","993","993","995","995","997","997","999","999"]}],"solution":"class TimeMap:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.times = defaultdict(list)   # key -> sorted timestamps\n        self.values = defaultdict(list)  # key -> values, parallel to times\n\n    def set(self, key: str, value: str, timestamp: int) -> None:\n        self.times[key].append(timestamp)\n        self.values[key].append(value)\n\n    def get(self, key: str, timestamp: int) -> str:\n        if key not in self.times:\n            return ''\n        i = bisect_right(self.times[key], timestamp)\n        return self.values[key][i - 1] if i else ''\n","approach":"**Key insight: the history of each key is already sorted, so reads are a binary search.** Writes arrive with strictly increasing timestamps per key, which means appending to a per-key list keeps it sorted with no extra work.\n\nKeep a dictionary from key to two parallel lists (timestamps and values), or a single list of pairs. `set` is an O(1) append. `get` uses `bisect_right(times, timestamp)`, which returns how many stored timestamps are <= the query; if that count is zero the key had no value yet, otherwise the answer is at index `count - 1`.\n\n**Common mistakes:** using `bisect_left`, which returns the wrong index when the query equals a stored timestamp; returning the most recent value regardless of the query time; linear scans, which are O(n) per get and time out under 2 * 10^5 calls.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** What if timestamps are *not* guaranteed increasing? (use `insort` for O(n) inserts, or a balanced tree / sorted containers for O(log n).) How would you scale this past one machine? (shard by key; each shard keeps its own sorted history. This is essentially how versioned KV stores and MVCC work.) How would you bound memory? (retention policy: drop versions older than a cutoff, or keep only the last k versions per key.)","complexity":{"time":"O(1) set, O(log n) get where n is the number of writes to that key","space":"O(total writes)"},"similar":["snapshot-array","lru-cache"],"number":181}